{"type":"message","id":"6d0b9889","parentId":"887a7f1d","timestamp":"2026-02-18T03:53:21.192Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-02-18 09:23 GMT+5:30] Fix gateway instability: crashes/shuts down on restart.\n\n**Simple approach:**\n1. Check for stale lock file at `D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\.openclaw-state\\openclaw.lock` — if exists and PID not running, delete it.\n2. Run `openclaw doctor --non-interactive` and fix any config errors it reports.\n3. Ensure no process is holding port 18789 (kill if zombie).\n4. Restart gateway with `openclaw gateway restart`.\n5. Verify it stays up for at least 30 seconds.\n\nIf you find a specific error in logs (look in `.openclaw-state/logs/` or run `openclaw logs --tail 100`), report it and apply minimal fix.\n\n**Deliverable:** One- or two-sentence summary of what you fixed. Example: \"Deleted stale lock file that prevented clean start\" or \"Fixed port conflict by freeing port 18789\".\n\nWrite the summary to `gateway-crash-fix.md` in workspace root."}],"timestamp":1771386801188}}
